    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="0743" n="731" xml:id="pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.8595/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-11T17:00:00-03:00">March 11, 1942—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>797. Aranha<anchor n="7" xml:id="d690-f1"/> tells me that the Government has
                    ordered all Brazilian boats to take refuge in nearest ports. He says that they
                    will arm those in Brazilian ports. He asks if we can do anything about helping
                    to arm those in United States ports.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d690-f1" n="7" xml:id="d690-f1-content">
                <p>Oswaldo Aranha, Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
